hat the excess  material goes wasted so you would have  to say that each tape can produce 22  whole ribbons  from there  we know that we need 200 total ribbons  so we divide that by the 22 ribbons per  tape to get that we'll need 9 plus 1  over 11 tapes  in other words we'll need more than 9  tapes since 9 tapes are too few we will  need 10 tapes to produce all the 200  ribbons  so this is a fairly tricky question  and getting to the correct answer of 10  tapes requires  some thoughtful process of considering  the dimensions  and the excess material of each tape  did you figure out this problem  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel i make videos on  math you can catch me on my blog mind  your decisions which you can follow on  facebook google plus and patreon you can  catch me on social media at  preshtalwalker and if you like this  video please check out my books there  are links in the video description
 

